## Reading the ledger

```bash
# spend per tier this month
jq -s 'group_by(.tier)[] | {tier: .[0].tier, agents: length, tok: (map(.tokens.total) | add)}' \
   telemetry/usage-$(date +%Y-%m).jsonl

# every spawn the routing hook had to upgrade — a hand-written model that broke the ladder
jq -c 'select(.upgraded)' telemetry/spawns-*.jsonl

# how often did `auto` reclassify, and into what
jq -c 'select(.strategy != null) | {issue, strategy, tier}' telemetry/spawns-*.jsonl | sort -u
```

The last one is the calibration question: if tickets keep being reclassified into the same surface, that surface belongs in the entry table of [[feedback-loop-strategy-profiles]] — a change a **human** makes, so the next ticket enters at the right rung instead of paying for the discovery.
